{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And behind the door.</b> Likewise in secret." "<b>You set your remembrance.</b> Like וְזָכְרוּ כֵּין לְבָנוֹן (Hosea 14:8), and from the same root אַזְכָּרָה (Leviticus 2:2)." "<b>For from me [you exposed].</b> Like a harlot, for you exposed yourself from me — I who used to conceal you." "<b>And you went up.</b> To commit harlotry publicly." "<b>You widened your bed.</b> The sense is that the bed would accommodate many men." "<b>And you cut for yourself from them.</b> In place of וְכָרַתִּי, and similarly וַתַּעֲשִׂי הָרָע וַתּוּכַל (Jeremiah 3:5). וְכָרַתִּי לָּךְ בְּרִית מֵהֶם — you chose them to be the men of your covenant." "<b>[The love of their bed].</b> Those whom you loved to lie with you." "<b>A hand you envisioned.</b> In every place that you saw — like בְּכָל מָקוֹם אֲשֶׁר תִּרְאֶה (Deuteronomy 12:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {7 "The bracketed phrase 'בכל מקום אשר תראה' is cited as a gloss clarifying the idiom 'יד חזית'; the bracketed text appears to be Ibn Ezra's parenthetical illustration."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:03.151242691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}